  "_doc": {
    "about": "Encrypted sends with Bcc: one message for To and Cc, one per Bcc recipient, so no recipient sees a Bcc recipient's key id. Every client must match. Contract: docs/pgp-contract.md (Sending). Strings use CRLF where messages do.",
    "plan": "planEncryptedSends(input) == expect. Addresses in encryptTo are addressKey form (trimmed, lower-case); the sender's own key is added by the caller, never listed.",
    "protect": "The messages of the second plan entry, built with buildMime (compose-fixtures' rules, boundary token fixture2): protectedParts(mime, { bccCopy }) == { outerHeaders, inner }. A Bcc copy keeps To and Cc only inside and has Bcc both inside and outside."
  },
